## 3. Folder & File Structure

### Root Directory
* `my-app/` - Contains the React frontend application code.
* `server/` - Contains the Node.js Express backend API code.
* `ai_engine/` - Contains the Python Flask NLP parsing & SQL generation service.

### Frontend (`my-app/`)
* `src/components/` - Highly structured UI grouping.
  - `auth/` - Contains `LoginForm.jsx`, `SignupForm.jsx`, `VerifyPage.jsx`, `ForgotPassword.jsx`.
  - `business/` - Represents Vault/Business selection `BusinessForm.jsx`, `List.jsx`.
  - `accounts/` - Ledger Accounts logic (`CreateNewAccount.jsx`, `ShowBusinessAccount.jsx`, `EditAccount.jsx`).
  - `transactions/` - Adding/Viewing/Editing Double-Entry records.
  - `reports/` - Advanced derived tables (`LedgerBalancing.jsx`, `IncomeReport.jsx`, `TrialBalance.jsx`, `BalanceSheet.jsx`).
  - `chat/` - `FloatingChatbot.jsx` UI and styling for AI module.
* `src/contexts/` - `BusinessContext.jsx` manages the global state for the currently selected business context. PrivateRoute ensures authenticated boundaries.
* `src/App.jsx` - Main router defining URL paths to UI components.

### Backend (`server/`)
* `server.js` - Project entry point. Express app config, CORS, Session setups, and Router mounting.
* `db.js` - MySQL Pool configuration and connection loader.
* `auth.js` - Passport.js implementation logic for Google SSO handling.
* `routers/` - All individual Express endpoints compartmentalized (e.g., `aiRoutes.js`, `balanceSheet.js`, `incomeReport.js`, `transactionApi.js`).
* `controllers/` - `aiController.js` serves as the intermediary controller handling requests before routing to the Python microservice.

### AI Engine (`ai_engine/`)
* `app.py` - Flask server exposing the `/generate-sql` route.
* `parser.py` - Uses `spaCy` to map user language into `intent`, `intent_tables`, and filters (`dates`, `amounts`).
* `query_builder.py` - Maps parsed intents into strict read-only SQL queries to protect the db while dynamically selecting context points.
* `metadata.py` - Preloaded static FAQs vs dynamic DB schema maps.

